WEBVTT

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:09.500
Man, it's been a long time since 
I went on a trip to the Hot Springs.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.630
Thanks a bunch for inviting me along, Tadokoro.

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:15.660
Yeah, For occasions like these, 
it's a lot more enjoyable if everyone went.

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:16.960
But you know....

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:20.760
Is it really okay to bring this many people?

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:25.660
Um... the Inn keeper gave me the "Okay", 
so I think we should be fine.

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:29.260
If they're all Megumi-chan's friends, no matter 
how many of them are, they're all welcome.

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:33.460
After all during the Stagiaire, you did an 
excellent job working at our Inn.

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:36.330
N-N-N-No way... T-Thank you very much!

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:38.930
Megumi seems to be really liked.

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:42.060
Well of course. Back at home we bragged about her.

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:45.260
But is it really okay to bring me along?

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:47.960
Yeah, Doesn't it feel like we're imposing?

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:52.660
But, when Yukihira-kun invited you,
 you looked really happy, right?

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:55.730
T-That's not.. That's not true!!

00:00:55.730 --> 00:01:00.930
When Yukihira told me to come, I thought for 
sure we were going to do a Shokugeki match.

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:03.760
Are challenges the only thing that goes on in your mind?

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:07.160
Then why the hell are you here, bastard?

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:08.860
I...

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:10.930
<i>You were invited to the Hot Spring?!</i>

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:13.530
<i>Then that means you were able to make friends?</i>

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:17.960
<i>All right! You did it Hayama-kun!! Sensei is super happy.</i>

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:19.960
<i>Go our and have as much fun as you can!!</i>

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:23.060
<i>After being told so happily...</i>

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:25.860
Going to the hot spring together! Hot spring as an event!

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:27.060
This is the school life!

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:28.260
This is friendship!

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:30.630
This is youth, all right!

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:32.960
We'll arrive at the Inn in about five minutes.

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:36.760
You can go fishing in this area too?

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:39.660
Yes. It's a really good spot.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:44.360
There's this one that the fishers always aim for.
It's even got its own name, "This River's Master"

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:48.930
The River's Master?

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:22.540
A meeting in the Fall

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:24.100
Inn keeper, thank you very much for your inviting us today.

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:28.560
Welcome. Today it'll be just Megumi-chan and your friends alone.

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:30.460
So enjoy your stay to the fullest.

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:31.660
Yes!

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:34.130
Secret Move: Smoking Drive!

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:36.330
Knowledge Cut!

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:40.360
Oh! I just saw an image of a book for a split second!

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:43.960
Knowledge and smokes have nothing to do with this though.

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:54.030
Hmm...

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:55.630
All right!

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:57.530
Aw man, I lost!

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.960
Everyone seems to be fired up already.

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:03.160
Ah. That's one of the Polar Star's Seven Wonders.

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:06.360
It's Isshiki-senpai's "<i>By the time I noticed it, he was in a fundoshi</i>" illusion.

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:06.960
Right?

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:09.860
The Seventh Seat's mysterious power, huh?

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:10.660
You're wrong.

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:13.560
It's been a while, so how about it, Tadokoro-chan?

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:16.130
Yes. I've already prepared myself.

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:16.560
Eh?

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:19.930
Tadokoro, what's with that outfit?

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:22.930
Huh? I mean if you're wearing a yukata...

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:26.760
You can't play for real.

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:37.430
This isn't the Tadokoro I know.

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:40.460
Megumi started playing ping-pong during primary school.

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:45.630
In half a year, she didn't lose against kids her age. After that she won countless tournaments.

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:51.360
She was nicknamed "Tohoku's Hopping  Hare". There isn't anyone in her hometown that doesn't know her.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.200
[Shokugeki no Soma]   is a cooking manga

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.130
Alright!

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:56.360
If there's anyone who can scare Megumi in the dorm...

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:57.330
That would be...

00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:59.560
...Isshiki-senpai alone!

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:05.360
Amazing!

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:10.360
Isshiki-senpai seems to be intermingling returns with the rubber side to shake Megumi.

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:15.130
However, Megumi always turns them neutral again and she hasn't neglected her for hand shots either.

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:16.000
As expected from her.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.960
I don't understand a thing you're saying.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:22.460
All right!

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:24.130
It's Megumi's match point!

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:26.260
Isshiki-senpai has no way out!

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:34.730
<i>Kuh... Isn't there anything? Think! Think!</i>

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:37.330
<i>An underhanded move that will turn this match around!</i>

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:39.110
[Shokugeki no Soma]   is a cooking manga

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:41.300
<i>Eh? What did you say?</i>

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:42.000
Huh?

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:43.160
Inn keeper?

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:43.830
Here.

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:45.560
Sorry, let me go take a look.

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:49.460
Then is there anyone else that would like to face me?

00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:54.960
I'm glad that I came along with you, Erina.

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:59.200
You're pusy as always even though I told you this was for work.

00:05:56.550 --> 00:05:57.160
<i>Yes</i>

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:00.460
<i>I'm counting on you.</i>

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:03.460
But Ryou-kun up and left all of a sudden and I was bored!

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:07.260
Erina-sama. Today's plan seems to be taken care of.

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:08.760
Thank you, Hisako.

00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:10.260
What about to the rest of the wor-

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:13.030
Jeez! Erina, you work too much!

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:17.030
The Autumn Election and Stagiaire is long over, so you need to take a long break!

00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:18.300
But...

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:19.160
I agree.

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.430
It looks like we're free until tomorrow.

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:23.860
Rest is just as important once in a while.

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:28.530
And I'd also like to enter the hot springs with you, Erina-sama.

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:32.960
You're right. If you say so, Hisako...

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:36.600
And of course I brought them with me. Cards!

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:44.100
Today it's not only Ryouko, but even Nikumi-cchi...

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:46.500
This is... This is...

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:49.260
Unfair!!!

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:52.530
like I thought it's the meat! It's because you have the meat's power, right?!

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:56.000
Even though I have the meat's power...

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:57.360
Um...

00:06:57.370 --> 00:06:58.800
Don't mind her, Mito-san.

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:01.600
Yuki's always like this whenever we enter the bath.

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:04.460
Even so, Megumi's really slow.

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:13.260
We have hot springs in Italy, but the hot springs in Japan are so nice and spacious, right brother?

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:14.360
You're right, Isami.

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:18.130
What's wrong?

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:20.630
No... Yukihira doesn't seem to be here.

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:25.700
Ah. Yukihira just left with Hayama and Kurokiba.

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:29.030
Ah. They were talking about a battle or something.

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:30.060
A battle?!

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:32.330
Leaving someone like me behind?!

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:35.830
The only one who can battle against Yukihira first is me!

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:41.260
He's always like that so it's fine to leave him alone.

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:45.660
It looks like you can find this and that up here in the mountains...

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:49.330
And with the fishing rods we borrowed  from the old man, how about a having a cooking showdown here?

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:51.260
It's my guaranteed win then.

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:53.200
Who's going to be judge then?

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.630
I don't see a problem if we tasted the dishes ourselves.

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:57.800
Can we even call this a match anymore?

00:07:57.800 --> 00:08:00.230
My win is guaranteed then.

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:06.230
Apparently there's this "<i>River Master</i>". So whoever hooks the fish first gets 10 points!

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:08.660
Like I said, what kind of rules are those?!

00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:12.060
My win is surely set in stone!

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:12.150
Berserk Mode

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:15.240
I'm on a whole new level then you guys!

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:17.260
For example, what do you call this?

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:18.900
Eh? A Net?

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:19.650
It's a brailing scoop!

00:08:20.170 --> 00:08:21.060
What about this?

00:08:21.070 --> 00:08:21.730
A fishing rod?

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:22.630
An extended pole!

00:08:23.170 --> 00:08:24.530
This is just a quiz.

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:27.300
You can't tell our fishing skills like this.

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:30.460
Well you're right about that.

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:32.500
That's what you're honest about?

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:35.660
You guys sure are weird.

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:37.160
Don't compare me to you.

00:08:37.170 --> 00:08:38.330
Like you can talk.

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:39.460
Eh?

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:41.830
That' really neat!

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:44.660
The spring water here is supposedly good for your skin.

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:47.930
Our skin became all smooth and silky-

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:49.730
Ouch, ouch, ouch!!

00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:52.260
Are you okay? You shouldn't push yourself...

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:53.460
What's wrong?

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:55.300
Ah! Everyone!

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:57.060
We're terribly sorry for all the ruckus.

00:08:57.630 --> 00:08:59.930
Our fish cook sprained his back, you see.

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:01.430
I-I can get through this with guts-

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:03.330
Ouch, ouch, ouch!

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:06.830
Um, like I thought, please allow me to help with you anything!

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:10.800
You're right. All of our other stand-ins were constantly injured.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:14.330
All of them either sprained their ankle, broke their bone, and fell.

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:16.400
Our entire staff was wiped out.

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:18.000
Wiped out?

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:18.960
A curse?

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:19.960
It's just a coincidence, right?

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:24.130
And here's the problem. Our third got the wrong date and invited other guests else to the Inn.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:28.130
In that case don't you think we'd be all the more helpful to you?

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:32.560
We have this many cooks to spare. Please let us help you.

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:36.460
We're students from Tohtsuki Academy who's survived past to the Stagiaire.

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:38.130
You can rely on all of us!

00:09:38.530 --> 00:09:39.630
I'll help out too!

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:40.830
Please allow us to help.

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:41.660
You can leave everything to us!

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:45.060
Please! Inn Keeper!!

00:09:45.530 --> 00:09:48.760
We should be the ones. We're counting on you.

00:09:49.370 --> 00:09:50.700
Welcome! Thank you for coming!

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:52.460
I'll guide you to your rooms.

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:55.760
Thank you for your hard work. We'll leave it to you.

00:09:55.770 --> 00:09:57.400
We'll been in your care.

00:09:57.400 --> 00:09:59.030
This is a nice place.

00:09:59.430 --> 00:10:02.830
Getting a reservation at this Inn was super hard work, you know!

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:07.060
Where are you? Where are you? Where are you, Yukihira?!

00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:10.800
Yukihiraaaa!!!!!

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:17.330
No one seems to coming back yet.

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:29.330
This feels so nice!!!!

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:33.960
Like I thought, washing all of your fatigue away is nice, isn't it Erina-sama?

00:10:33.970 --> 00:10:37.900
Yes. How long has it been since I've felt this relaxing feeling I wonder?

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:41.830
Apparently this Inn has various other types of baths as well...

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:43.360
We have to try them all out!

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:46.330
I don't see the need to enter all the baths

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:50.630
As always Erina, you're inexperienced with a lot of things!

00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:54.300
At the hot springs your supposed to enjoy and soak yourself

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:55.530
I-Is that so?

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:59.230
Erina-sama, before that, dinner time is approaching.

00:10:59.570 --> 00:11:01.460
Oh, is that so?

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:04.530
I wonder if the food will be delicious, Hishoko-chan.

00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:05.660
Who are you calling Hishoko?!!

00:11:06.070 --> 00:11:08.660
Especially for the 10th seat's...

00:11:08.970 --> 00:11:13.260
Erina's God's Tongue. I wonder if they can they satisfy it?

00:11:18.970 --> 00:11:20.560
That's a pretty tiny one.

00:11:21.230 --> 00:11:23.760
You haven't caught a single thing yet, haven't you?

00:11:24.270 --> 00:11:29.760
Fishing is a Man's Battlefield! If you don't have the guts, you're just snack to a fish!

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:32.830
You say that, but you haven't caught a single thing yet.

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:35.160
You said you had this equipment down, right?

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:38.760
It is my first time fishing here in a river.

00:11:38.770 --> 00:11:40.260
I can't find a comeback for this.

00:11:40.270 --> 00:11:42.930
Isn't it tiring to take your bandanna off and on all the time?

00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:47.160
Looks like something good took bait!

00:11:49.570 --> 00:11:50.460
Be careful, Yukihira!

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:52.860
Oh, Hayama! Sorry...

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:54.900
Hey, could this one be...

00:11:57.130 --> 00:11:58.300
The River's Master!!

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:01.360
Kurokiba! Stop looking and help us!

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:02.100
Grab the net!

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:05.330
Net? Oh, you mean the brailing scoop?

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:06.830
Before that put on the your bandanna!!

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:12.660
Hurry! Time is running short!

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:15.600
I'm almost done with preparations over here.

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:17.060
I just have a bit more until I'm finished.

00:12:17.430 --> 00:12:19.430
I'll show you that my current new skills.

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:23.760
I'm terribly sorry, because of me this wouldn't have happened...

00:12:24.070 --> 00:12:27.060
No, we're all right. We'll make it on time.

00:12:27.070 --> 00:12:29.600
Leave frying the tempura to me!

00:12:30.070 --> 00:12:32.060
"<i>Mukozuke Seasonal Sashimi</i>", is done!

00:12:32.670 --> 00:12:35.530
Oh, you're going with that for dessert?

00:12:35.530 --> 00:12:35.900
Yeah.

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:39.060
I thought it would be a good idea.

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:40.730
Looks delicious!

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:48.930
Don't Waver!!!!

00:12:50.930 --> 00:12:55.760
The bath is so lonely.
I wonder where everyone left to go?

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:03.730
The appetizer course are here.

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:05.630
Please take your time and enjoy your meal.

00:13:06.070 --> 00:13:07.130
Thank you for the meal.

00:13:08.570 --> 00:13:11.660
I was looking forward to the hot springs but like I thought, nothing beats the food here!

00:13:12.130 --> 00:13:13.300
Thank you for the meal.

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:15.260
Thank you for the meal.

00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:19.060
Oh! This is pretty good!

00:13:19.070 --> 00:13:20.930
These smoked mini tomatoes.

00:13:21.930 --> 00:13:23.850
Prince of Smoke

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:25.930
This is the soup course.

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:28.830
It feels like there's thousands of knowledge filled into one flavour.

00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:30.260
In this Japanese Shrimp Salad.

00:13:30.260 --> 00:13:33.230
The Professor of Taste.

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:35.860
Erina-sama, how is the taste for you?

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:43.100
My arms can't anymore!

00:13:43.100 --> 00:13:44.700
Don't waver yet Yukihira!

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:46.530
Not enough yet!

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:49.950
Little Red Ridding Hood of

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:49.950
the Forest of Wild Beasts.

00:13:50.230 --> 00:13:53.160
The dear meat combined with budu fish sauce...

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:56.660
It feels like the dish was fired from another country.

00:13:57.570 --> 00:13:59.530
Meat General.

00:14:00.070 --> 00:14:01.460
This grilled dish...

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:03.930
...gives you a fired up kind of feeling, right?

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:07.310
Flag bearers of the Fermentation

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:06.960
Bussiness the Sakaki Clan!

00:14:07.770 --> 00:14:09.560
The use of both mushrooms in the miso soup.

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:11.760
It seems to balance out really well.

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:21.300
Please let the people who eat this...
are left with a happy and nice felling.

00:14:28.370 --> 00:14:29.330
This is like...

00:14:30.230 --> 00:14:33.360
Japan's fairies that calm your heart in the bath.

00:14:34.030 --> 00:14:34.860
Yay!

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:38.860
Nuts of the gingko tree, chestnuts, accompanied with takikomi rice...

00:14:43.530 --> 00:14:45.160
These are made by novices, weren't they?

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:50.860
But they was made carefully and they were dishes you can thoroughly enjoy.

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:54.860
For example you can say that the baths in this Inn,

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:57.760
were made just for viewing the shining moon and the falling red leaves.

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:04.830
It what are guest said about each dish.

00:15:05.270 --> 00:15:07.760
All right! We did it!

00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:17.510
<i>Polar Star! Polar Star! Polar Star!</i>

00:15:09.730 --> 00:15:12.000
Now that I feel relieved, I'm getting hungry.

00:15:12.700 --> 00:15:14.760
Let's start eating then.

00:15:14.770 --> 00:15:15.160
Yeah.

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:17.260
I'm famished!

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:18.260
Good work!

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:19.660
Everyone put in their best effort.

00:15:20.130 --> 00:15:22.560
I see. So That's what it was.

00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:24.530
This is youth!

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:27.060
Drink up, drink up! It's rice juice!!

00:15:32.230 --> 00:15:34.460
It's finally our turn to enter the hot springs.

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:38.600
How pretty.

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:44.630
I wonder if our cooking left today's guest with a good feeling like this one.

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:48.400
Ya-hoo! It's fall!

00:15:48.410 --> 00:15:50.060
It is...

00:15:50.230 --> 00:15:52.360
This gets me fired up

00:15:54.290 --> 00:15:55.460
Yukihira?!

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:57.500
Kurokiba-kun and Hayama-kun, too?

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:59.930
Now that I think about it, the three of you weren't around this whole time!

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:01.600
Oh, it's Nikumi.

00:16:03.030 --> 00:16:05.000
Y-You...! W-What were you doing until now?

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:07.360
Well... about that...

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:11.060
The River's Master was pretty hard opponent.

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:20.160
And in the end it got away.

00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:21.660
Hah?

00:16:21.670 --> 00:16:22.900
That sounds rough.

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:24.910
Are you an idiot?

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:27.630
Huh?

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:32.560
Hu? Duck-chan? Duck-chan? Where are you?
Duck-chan? Duck-chan?

00:16:32.570 --> 00:16:35.700
What should I do? Duck-chan!!

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:37.700
Are you perhaps talking about this little one?

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:41.730
Nakiri-san?

00:16:42.670 --> 00:16:45.260
Tadokoro-san! What a coincidence meeting you out here.

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.330
Yeah, I was suprised.

00:16:48.970 --> 00:16:51.160
Then today's guest was...!

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:54.660
Are you all right? Have you been in the water too long?

00:16:54.670 --> 00:16:56.560
No, no. I'm okay!

00:16:58.670 --> 00:17:03.130
I see! So that's how it is.
The one who praised our cooking was...

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:06.660
This feels so nice.

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:07.760
It does.

00:17:08.530 --> 00:17:10.930
It's feels like your heart is set flying here.

00:17:13.770 --> 00:17:18.830
We couldn't finish the cooking match, but we can gain some experience from that failure.

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:20.960
You were just fooling around.

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:23.260
An entire day wasted on something meaningless.

00:17:23.970 --> 00:17:25.530
But it was fun, right?

00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:30.960
And it's frustrating but I lost to Hayama again.

00:17:31.670 --> 00:17:32.660
In a fishing competition.

00:17:33.670 --> 00:17:34.960
I don't feel like I won.

00:17:35.770 --> 00:17:37.400
I don't feel like I lost either.

00:17:37.770 --> 00:17:39.560
Next time I'll win for sure!

00:17:41.470 --> 00:17:41.830
What?

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:44.130
I hear Milady's voice.

00:17:45.030 --> 00:17:48.930
Let me go, Hishoko-chan!
I have to enter every bath here!

00:17:48.930 --> 00:17:52.730
You mustn't Milady! Right now it's the boys turn to take a bath!

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:54.200
I'm coming in!

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:55.130
Milady!!!

00:17:56.070 --> 00:17:59.060
Where are you? Where are you?
Where are you, Yukihira?!

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:03.260
Yukihiraaaaa!!!!

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:40.860
Is that you, Takumi?

00:19:40.870 --> 00:19:42.760
Yukihira!

00:19:43.230 --> 00:19:43.760
Yeah.

00:19:44.170 --> 00:19:45.960
I finally found you!

00:19:45.970 --> 00:19:47.960
Welcome home, brother.

00:19:47.970 --> 00:19:49.660
Oh Isami. I'm home.

00:19:50.430 --> 00:19:52.130
Where have you been this whole time?

00:19:52.130 --> 00:19:54.130
Where have you been this time, Yukihira?!

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:57.260
Don't go worrying me like that all the time, jeez!

00:19:57.270 --> 00:20:02.130
And if we're talking about the cooking battle, all you have to do is call out and give the order.

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:06.060
Listen Yukihira. In the close future, you will have a battle with me!

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:07.860
Y-Yeah.

00:20:08.230 --> 00:20:11.730
Yukihira, do you know what struggles I went through to search for you?!

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:14.560
Listen, I'm super, super angry, you know?!!

00:20:14.570 --> 00:20:15.960
I got it, I got it!

00:20:19.050 --> 00:20:21.000
HAPPY TO SERVE!

00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:24.660
Yukihira, hasn't your hair grown a bit longer?

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:26.160
You think so?

00:20:26.630 --> 00:20:27.560
Youth!

00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:29.630
Disgusting!

00:20:38.870 --> 00:20:40.630
They don't go together at all.

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:42.160
Squid tentacles and peanut butter...

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:44.800
I can't help but laugh.

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:46.430
It's so disgusting I can't help but laugh!

00:20:48.630 --> 00:20:52.030
This isn't a laughing matter, Yukihira-kun!
Just looking at you defiles my tongue!

00:20:52.670 --> 00:20:54.760
As an apology you will make a dish with egg as the main ingredient.

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:57.860
If you make a dish that will satisfy my palette, I'll forgive you.

00:20:57.870 --> 00:20:59.460
What's with this half-assed turned of events?

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:05.560
Tsukuda-sensei couldn't think of a better story so don't complain.

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:06.860
Are you going to do it? Or not?

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:08.230
I guess it can't be helped.

00:21:08.970 --> 00:21:10.760
Anything I want? Like a seaweed-bento?

00:21:10.770 --> 00:21:13.000
I told you the main ingredient has to be an egg.

00:21:15.300 --> 00:21:17.930
Hang onto your seat, Examiner Nakiri.

00:21:19.470 --> 00:21:21.060
Eggs are a fundamental ingredient.
